## Why This Is Asked

Covers a realistic data-leak risk from IAM misconfig in pipelines, focusing on formal CAPA processes at a beginner level.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data modeling
- Lifecycle state machines
- Evidence-driven REST APIs
- Metrics for containment and prevention
- RCA templates and canary-based remediation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal Express route to POST /caps
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let caps = [];
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const cap = { id: Date.now().toString(), ...req.body };
  caps.push(cap);
  res.status(201).json(cap);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you secure the CAPA API (authorization, audit logs, idempotency)?
- How would you integrate with existing incident response tools?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a CAPA for data-quality failures in a multi-region streaming system, focusing on traceable evidence, lifecycle consistency, and measurable containment.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model design with domain-appropriate fields
- Lifecycle state machine for incident progression
- Minimal REST API contract for creating/updating CAPAs with evidence
- Region-aware metrics to prove containment and prevent recurrence
- RCA templates and canary-based remediation strategies

